{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQVyZigD1ry3p8PTJBVDGA","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (90.3KB). Full output saved to: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Jyue-Documents-1-projects-noss-to-wim\\390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9\\tool-results\\b2havuhy3.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n## Codebase Patterns\r\n\r\n- PA.md files live in each CU folder (e.g. aesthetic-services/C04/PA.md)\r\n- Tests use Path(__file__).parent.parent for PROJECT_ROOT, read .md files directly\r\n- Keep PA documents under 250 lines with compact markdown tables to avoid diff-guard limits\r\n- WIM modality reference tables use: Modality | Frequency | Intensity | Duration | KP Ref columns\r\n- Bilingual format: English term (*Bahasa Malaysia term*) inline\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Ralph Progress Log - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  2:45:02 PM\r\nStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-001 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is a technical writing task, not a Frappe/Python coding task. The agent's work will be focused on updating content within Markdown files.\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief for Agent**\r\n\r\n*   **Objective:** Enhance the technical accuracy and depth of High Voltage (HV) safety procedures in BEV Information Sheets.\r\n*   **Files to Modify:**\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-01.md`\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-02.md`\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-03.md`\r\n*   **Frappe/Python Involvement:** None. The story does not pertain to Python code, Frappe DocTypes, or hooks. The task is purely content and documentation based.\r\n*   **Implementation Approach:**\r\n    1.  **Research Regulations:** Review content to ensure it aligns with Malaysia's OSHA 1994 and EQA 1974, plus specific BEV manufacturer standards.\r\n    2.  **Verify PPE:** Update Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) details to be precise for BEV Level 3 work, specifically mentioning Class 0 gloves and CAT-III multimeter requirements.\r\n    3.  **Add Bilingual Terms:** For key technical concepts, ensure both English (EN) and Bahasa Malaysia (BM) terms are present.\r\n    4.  **Cite Sources:** Add references or footnotes to link claims to the correct regulations.\r\n*   **Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\r\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9","uuid":"63adf050-cc55-47c3-9d3a-a2afda40d73b","timestamp":"2026-04-17T02:45:17.038Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Codebase Patterns\r\n\r\n- PA.md files live in each CU folder (e.g. aesthetic-services/C04/PA.md)\r\n- Tests use Path(__file__).parent.parent for PROJECT_ROOT, read .md files directly\r\n- Keep PA documents under 250 lines with compact markdown tables to avoid diff-guard limits\r\n- WIM modality reference tables use: Modality | Frequency | Intensity | Duration | KP Ref columns\r\n- Bilingual format: English term (*Bahasa Malaysia term*) inline\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Ralph Progress Log - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  2:45:02 PM\r\nStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-001 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is a technical writing task, not a Frappe/Python coding task. The agent's work will be focused on updating content within Markdown files.\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief for Agent**\r\n\r\n*   **Objective:** Enhance the technical accuracy and depth of High Voltage (HV) safety procedures in BEV Information Sheets.\r\n*   **Files to Modify:**\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-01.md`\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-02.md`\r\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-03.md`\r\n*   **Frappe/Python Involvement:** None. The story does not pertain to Python code, Frappe DocTypes, or hooks. The task is purely content and documentation based.\r\n*   **Implementation Approach:**\r\n    1.  **Research Regulations:** Review content to ensure it aligns with Malaysia's OSHA 1994 and EQA 1974, plus specific BEV manufacturer standards.\r\n    2.  **Verify PPE:** Update Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) details to be precise for BEV Level 3 work, specifically mentioning Class 0 gloves and CAT-III multimeter requirements.\r\n    3.  **Add Bilingual Terms:** For key technical concepts, ensure both English (EN) and Bahasa Malaysia (BM) terms are present.\r\n    4.  **Cite Sources:** Add references or footnotes to link claims to the correct regulations.\r\n*   **Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\r\n    *   **Diff Size Limit:** The previous attempt failed for creating too large of a diff. Apply changes incrementally and avoid reformatting entire documents to stay under the 500-line change limit.\r\n    *   **Regulatory Precision:** Ensure citations are to the specific, correct sections of the referenced Malaysian laws.\r\n    *   **Standards Accuracy:** Double-check that the PPE specifications are current and match industry best practices for HV electrical work.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-001 — Enhance BEV C01 KP technical depth — HV safety procedures and PPE specifications\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- KP-01: Updated safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard); added Electricity Supply Act 1990 (Act 447) to references with bilingual name\r\n- KP-02: Added bilingual heading for Digital Multimeter section; added IEC 61010-1 / MS IEC 61010-1 standard reference to DMM spec; added OSHA 1994 (Act 514), EQA 1974 (Act 127), ESA 1990 (Act 447) to References\r\n- KP-03: Added OSHA 1994 and ESA 1990 citations at start of safety section; added explicit PPE table with Class 0 gloves, CAT-III multimeter, MS ISO 16321 glasses; added BM term for LOTO (Kunci-Keluar/Tag-Keluar); added Malaysian regulatory references\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- diff size anti-pattern: previous attempt generated 2183 lines by rewriting entire files. Correct approach: surgical edits only (66 lines total)\r\n- KP-01 was already mostly compliant; focused changes were just adding the missing Electricity Supply Act ref and updating safety glasses spec\r\n- CAT-III multimeter specification is a TOOL spec (not PPE), so only relevant in KP-02 (health check) and KP-03 (maintenance) — not KP-01 (workplace prep)\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Windows: must use encoding=utf-8 when opening files with Python\r\n- Malaysian standard for safety glasses is MS ISO 16321 (not DIN EN166)\r\n- Act numbers: OSHA = Act 514, EQA = Act 127, ESA = Act 447, Road Transport = Act 333\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-002 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-002: Enhance BEV Technical Knowledge Content**\r\n\r\n**Note:** The user story provided (US-002) is for enhancing Markdown-based technical documentation, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following brief is adjusted accordingly.\r\n\r\n**1. Target Files:**\r\nThis task involves modifying Markdown (`.md`) files, not Python code. The specific files are:\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-01.md`\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-02.md`\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-03.md`\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-04.md`\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-05.md`\r\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-06.md`\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe Context:**\r\nThere are no Frappe DocTypes or hooks involved. The work is confined to editing the content of the specified Markdown files.\r\n\r\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\r\nThe agent should read, analyze, and rewrite the content within each of the six KP files. The goal is to enhance the technical theory for BEV rectification, focusing on:\r\n- Battery Management System (BMS) components.\r\n- High-Voltage (HV) cable, On-Board Charger (OBC), and battery pack theory.\r\n- DC-DC converter function and failure modes.\r\n- Add clear descriptions for diagrams and include tables for component specifications.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n- **CRITICAL:** A previous attempt failed due to an `oversized_diff`. The agent must modify files incrementally. Process one file at a time to keep changes under the 5,000-line diff limit.\r\n- Ensure High-Voltage safety warnings are made prominent using Markdown callouts (e.g., `> **WARNING:** ...`).\r\n- Technical accuracy is paramount; content should be precise.\r\n- The scope is strictly limited to the content of the six listed files.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-002 — Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- KP-01: Fixed safety glasses spec (DIN EN166 → MS ISO 16321), added BMS component overview table with BM terms and failure modes column, added WARNING callout\r\n- KP-02: Added prominent WARNING callout for HV cable contact hazard, added HV cable/connector failure modes table\r\n- KP-03: Added WARNING callout for OBC residual HV risk, added OBC component specifications table (AC input, power ratings, cooling, communication)\r\n- KP-04: Added WARNING callout for pre-charge component hazards, added pre-charge system failure modes table (relay, resistor, contactor)\r\n- KP-05: Added WARNING callout with thermal runaway warning, added traction battery pack failure modes table\r\n- KP-06: Added WARNING callout for DC-DC HV input, converted prose failure symptoms to structured failure modes table\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- previous anti-pattern was oversized_diff (261,809 lines) from complete file rewrites. Correct approach: surgical additions only — 104 lines total for 6 files\r\n- WARNING callout pattern: `> **AMARAN / WARNING:** [specific hazard relevant to this component]` — each KP gets one targeted warning in the safety section\r\n- failure modes table pattern: | Component | Failure Mode | Symptom | Diagnosis | — 5-7 rows per file\r\n- specs table pattern: | Parameter | Specification | — placed after the definition/function section\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- KP-01 had DIN EN166 (European) instead of MS ISO 16321 (Malaysian standard) for safety glasses — same fix as C01\r\n- Each KP file already had good base content — surgical additions were sufficient, no rewrites needed\r\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:12:23 PM\r\nCompleted: Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory (ID: US-002) in 6m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-003 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is a content enhancement task, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following technical brief has been adjusted to reflect the actual task of modifying Markdown documentation.\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief: US-003 - BEV Knowledge Point Enhancement**\r\n\r\n1.  **Target Files (Content Modification):**\r\n    *   This is a documentation task; no Python files are involved.\r\n    *   The work involves editing Markdown (`.md`) files within the `bev-diagnostic-rectification/` directory.\r\n    *   Files for C03 (Thermal Cooling): `C03/KP-01.md`, `C03/KP-02.md`, `C03/KP-03.md`.\r\n    *   Files for C04 (Drive Train): `C04/KP-01.md` through `C04/KP-05.md`.\r\n\r\n2.  **Frappe/Application Context:**\r\n    *   No Frappe DocTypes, hooks, or server-side logic are applicable. The task is confined to the content layer of the knowledge base.\r\n\r\n3.  **Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n    *   For C03 KPs: Systematically review and enhance content on BEV thermal management. Ensure detailed descriptions of liquid cooling systems, components, and BEV-specific HVAC functions. Add troubleshooting theory.\r\n    *   For C04 KPs: Review and expand on the electric drive train. Detail the architecture, the role of inverters, theory of traction motors (AC induction vs. permanent magnet), and the principles of regenerative braking and brake control.\r\n\r\n4.  **Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n    *   **Primary Constraint:** All added content MUST align with \"manufacturer service manual standards.\" This requires a formal, precise, and technically accurate tone.\r\n    *   The content should remain theoretical (\"Knowledge Point\") and avoid becoming a step-by-step repair guide.\r\n    *   Ensure consistency in terminology (e.g., \"transaxle,\" \"inverter\") across all edited documents.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-003 — Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- C03/KP-01: Added WARNING callout for HV electric pump/compressor hazard; added dielectric coolant (cecair penyejuk dielektrik) awareness section with BM terms\r\n- C03/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for HV-connected cooling components; added cooling system failure modes table (6 rows: pump, hose, expansion tank, thermostat valve, heat exchanger, temp sensor)\r\n- C03/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for HV electric compressor; added heat pump system (sistem pam haba) theory section explaining efficiency vs PTC; renumbered subsections 2.3-2.6; added HVAC failure modes table (6 rows)\r\n- C04/KP-01: Added CU title heading; added WARNING callout covering inverter capacitor discharge hazard; added BM bilingual terms for key drive train components\r\n- C04/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for capacitor residual charge (10 min wait + 60V verification); added FOC/Vector Control theory section; added inverter specifications table (DC voltage, power, switching freq, efficiency)\r\n- C04/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for back-EMF hazard on motor phase cables; added regenerative braking theory section (generator mode, limitations table, blending); added motor failure modes table (6 rows)\r\n- C04/KP-04: Added WARNING callout for heavy HV e-axle assembly; added transaxle failure modes table (5 rows: gears, differential, seals, CV joints, lubricant)\r\n- C04/KP-05: Added WARNING callout for safety-critical system; added regenerative-friction blending table (6 conditions with contribution split); renumbered section 1.3→1.4\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Established pattern continues: each KP gets one WARNING callout at the top of the first content section, one failure modes table near the end, and one specifications/theory addition\r\n- Section renumbering is necessary when inserting new subsections — be careful to check sequential numbering\r\n- C04 files initially lacked CU heading — add it for consistency with C03 files\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- C03/KP-03 had subsections 2.2-2.5 that needed renumbering to 2.3-2.6 after inserting heat pump section as 2.2\r\n- Motor back-EMF warning is unique: even after HV isolation, moving the rotor generates voltage — important safety note not present in inverter KP\r\n- Regenerative braking limitations are a key theory point for C04: SOC, temperature, speed, ABS activation all disable or limit regeneration\r\n## Iteration 2 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:21:09 PM\r\nCompleted: Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory (ID: US-003) in 7m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-005 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\n**To:** Claude Code Agent\r\n**From:** Gemini\r\n**Subject:** Technical Brief for US-005: Enhance Practical Procedure DocType\r\n\r\nThis brief outlines the implementation for a user story on enhancing practical work procedures within the `lhdn_payroll_integration` custom Frappe app.\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files & DocTypes to Modify:**\r\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.py`: For server-side validation hooks.\r\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.js`: For client-side UI arrangement/validation.\r\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.json`: The primary DocType definition.\r\n*   Child DocTypes to create/update: `Procedure Step` and `Assessment Item`.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes and Hooks:**\r\n*   **Primary DocType:** A `Work Sheet` DocType to manage procedures. It should have `Text` or `Table` fields for `ppe_requirements`, `equipment_list`, and `safety_precautions`.\r\n*   **Child DocTypes:**\r\n    *   `Procedure Step`: A table containing step-by-step instructions.\r\n    *   `Assessment Item`: A table with a `Select` field for `domain` (Process, Output, Attitude, Safety, Environment) and a `Text` field for the assessment criteria.\r\n*   **Hooks (in work_sheet.py):**\r\n    *   `validate`: To enforce the acceptance criteria.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Update the `Work Sheet` DocType, ensuring `safety_precautions` is a separate field.\r\n2.  In `work_sheet.js`, use custom scripting to render the safety field prominently at the top of the form.\r\n3.  In `work_sheet.py`, implement the `validate` hook to check that the `Assessment Item` child table contains at least one entry for each of the five required domains before saving the document.\r\n4.  The logic should also verify that the `equipment_list` field is not empty.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   The story implies updating existing records. A patch script might be necessary to backfill data for the new checklist and equipment list structure in existing `Work Sheet` documents.\r\n*   The acceptance criterion for \"logical sequence\" is subjective; enforcing a numbered step sequence in the `Procedure Step` table is the most practical approach.\r\n*   Ensure any new mandatory fields have default values or are handled gracefully by the migration patch to avoid breaking existing records.\r\n\r\n## Story US-005 — Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- C01/KK-01, KK-02, KK-03: Fixed safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard)\r\n- C02/KK-01: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; expanded placeholder Step 2.1-2.5; restructured checklist to 5-domain structure with Remarks column\r\n- C02/KK-02: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; added numbered safety precautions list; restructured checklist to 5 domains\r\n- C02/KK-03: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; fixed AMARAN: format; added numbered safety precautions; restructured checklist to 5 domains\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- C01 KK files were well-structured but had DIN EN166 glasses spec error carried over from KP files\r\n- C02 KK files used compact inline lists instead of tables at initial creation\r\n- 5-domain checklist structure (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT) from C01 is the standard for all KK files\r\n- Assessment checklist requires Remarks column (5 columns total)\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- C02/KK-03 used AMARAN: without the / WARNING: bilingual suffix — always use AMARAN / WARNING: format\r\n- C02/KK-01 Step 2 was a placeholder referencing another file — must always expand placeholders before submission\r\n- Coolant in OBC work is SW305 scheduled waste — must appear in both safety precautions and ENVIRONMENT domain of checklist\r\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:38:23 PM\r\nCompleted: Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists (ID: US-005) in 9m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-007 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nHere is the technical brief for user story US-007.\r\n\r\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-007: Enhance Aesthetic KPs**\r\n\r\nThis story is a content enhancement task, not a Python coding task. The agent will review and update existing Markdown knowledge package (KP) files.\r\n\r\n**1. Target Files (Markdown, not Python):**\r\n- `aesthetic-services/C01/KP-01.md` through `KP-05.md`\r\n- `aesthetic-services/C02/KP-01.md` through `KP-07.md`\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks:**\r\n- No direct interaction with DocTypes or hooks is expected. The task is confined to updating the content of the specified `.md` files.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n- Read each target `.md` file.\r\n- Review content against acceptance criteria:\r\n    - C01: Correctness of consultation techniques, BMI calculation, body typing.\r\n    - C02: Accuracy of thermal therapy details, safety, and contraindications.\r\n- Enhance the text for anatomical and physiological accuracy.\r\n- Ensure all key concepts include required bilingual (English/local language) terminology.\r\n- Overwrite the existing files with the updated, reviewed content.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n- **Bilingual Accuracy:** This is a critical requirement. The agent must provide correct translations for technical terms.\r\n- **Subject-Matter Expertise:** The content is technical. The agent must ensure the information on anatomy, BMI, and thermal therapies is accurate and up-to-date.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-007 — Enhance Aesthetic C01-C02 KP — body consultation and thermal therapy theory\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- C01/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for disinfectant chemical hazards; enhanced magnifying lamp usage detail; added flexible measuring tape to tools table\r\n- C01/KP-03: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added calliper skinfold measurement sites table (4 sites with location + client position); added Waist-Hip Ratio (WHR) section with formula and risk classification table; renumbered 9.3 → 9.4 for Limitations\r\n- C02/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added thermal therapy modalities overview table with bilingual terms (6 modalities including body wrap)\r\n- C02/KP-02: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for electrical safety in thermal equipment room\r\n- C02/KP-05: Added body wrap (balutan badan) as modality 2.6 with full parameter table, procedure overview, and product types table; restructured section 4.0 with per-modality contraindications table and general precautions subsections\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- AMARAN / WARNING callout pattern established for BEV files applies identically to Aesthetic KP files\r\n- Body wrap was a critical missing modality — referenced in C01/KP-03 recommended treatments but not described in C02/KP-05 until this story\r\n- WHR (Waist-Hip Ratio) is the standard supplementary measure alongside BMI for body consultation — WHO cut-offs: women >0.85 = high risk, men >0.95 = high risk\r\n- Per-modality contraindication tables add significant value to C02/KP-05 — each modality has unique specific contraindications beyond the general list in C02/KP-01\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- C01/KP-03 section 9.3 needed renumbering to 9.4 after inserting WHR as new 9.3\r\n- Body wrap uses occlusive heat (no external heat source) — different physics from all other modalities\r\n- Calliper sites: 4 standard sites (triceps, subscapular, suprailiac, abdominal) — positions matter for accurate measurement\r\n\r\n## Story US-008 — Enhance Aesthetic C03 KP — manual body massage techniques and anatomy\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications; restructured into local/systemic/relative categories; expanded absolute contraindications (added anticoagulants, alcohol intoxication, psychosis, local contraindications section)\r\n- KP-02: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for massage medium allergy risk (nut-based carriers)\r\n- KP-03: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for professional draping standards\r\n- KP-04: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout; enhanced all 5 classical movements with hand position detail and tapotement sub-type table; added anatomy section 8.0 (major muscle groups by region, physiological effects table, anatomical landmarks to avoid)\r\n- KP-05: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for post-massage medical referral\r\n- KP-06: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for massage medium contamination prevention\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Contraindications for massage should be split 3 ways: systemic/absolute, local (area-avoid), relative — clearer than just absolute/relative\r\n- Tapotement has 5 sub-types with different hand positions — a table is the clearest format\r\n- Anatomy section belongs in KP-04 (the \"carry out\" KP) not KP-01 (consultation)\r\n- Anatomical landmarks to avoid (popliteal fossa, femoral triangle, carotid triangle, kidney region) are distinct from contraindications — warrant their own table\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Friction technique requires REMOVING medium first — the \"dry skin\" caution is critical to its effectiveness\r\n- Vibration is neurological (light pressure), not mechanical — different from all other movements\r\n- Anticoagulant medications (warfarin, heparin) are an absolute contraindication often missing from standard lists\r\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:59:53 PM\r\nCompleted: Enhance Aesthetic C03 KP — manual body massage techniques and anatomy (ID: US-008) in 9m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-009 — Enhance Aesthetic C04 KP — electrotherapy modalities (6 types) with safety\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING for electrical safety in work area (mains electricity, wet hands, damaged cables)\r\n- KP-02: Added AMARAN/WARNING before contraindications; expanded modality-specific table to include all 6 modalities including mechanical/gyratory (previously missing); added acute inflammation/fever to absolute list; enhanced reason descriptions\r\n- KP-03: Added AMARAN/WARNING with specific placements to avoid (thorax, carotid, cranium); added modality-specific contraindications at end of precautions\r\n- KP-04: Added AMARAN/WARNING for galvanic shock risk; added full procedure overview (was completely missing — only had precautions); added modality-specific contraindications\r\n- KP-05: Added AMARAN/WARNING for varicose vein risk; added lymph node drainage direction table (5 body areas); enhanced precautions with specific cup release technique; added modality-specific contraindications\r\n- KP-06: Added AMARAN/WARNING for stationary rotating head risk; enhanced precautions; added machine specifications table (motor type, RPM range, attachment type); added modality-specific contraindications\r\n- KP-07: Added AMARAN/WARNING for flammable products fire risk; added treatment parameters table comparing direct vs indirect method (was missing — only had precautions); enhanced precautions; added modality-specific contraindications\r\n- KP-08: Added AMARAN/WARNING for pacemaker risk even at sub-sensory levels; enhanced contraindications (added phlebitis, recent surgery); added machine specifications table; added note on dedicated micro-current gel requirement\r\n- KP-09: Added AMARAN/WARNING for adverse reaction referral protocol; enhanced aftercare table with specific durations; added modality-specific aftercare notes table (5 modalities)\r\n- KP-10: Added AMARAN/WARNING for clinical waste classification; restructured waste disposal into a classification table with 7 waste types; added inventory management section with FIFO and stock count procedures\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- KP-04 (Galvanic) was missing a procedure overview entirely — all other modality KPs had one. Galvanic is unique in requiring polarity check before product application\r\n- KP-07 (High Frequency) was missing a parameters table — critical because direct and indirect methods have completely different applications, yet shared the same machine output\r\n- Mechanical/gyratory was missing from the modality-specific contraindications table in KP-02 — the 6th modality was not represented\r\n- Micro-current requires dedicated conductive gel — not standard conductive gel — a frequently missed clinical detail\r\n- High frequency fire hazard from flammable products is a critical safety point often understated in training materials\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Galvanic shock (from moving electrode without zeroing current) is distinct from electrical burns — it is a sharp pain event caused by sudden current change\r\n- Vacuum suction stationary cup → petechiae (pin-point bruising) is the most common client complaint — must be explained in aftercare\r\n- High frequency direct method: electrode on skin BEFORE switching on (not after) — prevents sparking on initial contact\r\n- Micro-current: pacemaker contraindication applies even at sub-sensory levels because demand-type pacemakers can interpret micro-currents as cardiac signals\r\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026 10:17:39 PM\r\nCompleted: Enhance Aesthetic C04 KP — electrotherapy modalities (6 types) with safety (ID: US-009) in 10m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-012 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis technical brief is for a Claude Code agent tasked with implementing user story US-012 within the `lhdn_payroll_integration` Frappe app.\r\n\r\n**Objective:** Implement a validation system to ensure \"Aesthetic KK\" procedure documents, which are referenced by a Frappe DocType, contain all required sections and details.\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Modify:**\r\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/hooks.py`: To hook the validation logic into a DocType event.\r\n*   `[app]/[doctype]/[doctype].py`: The controller file for the DocType managing the procedures (e.g., `Aesthetic Procedure`). This will house the main validation method.\r\n*   A new utility file (e.g., `lhdn_payroll_integration/utils/validator.py`) could be created to contain the specific Markdown parsing and checking logic, keeping the controller lean.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes & Hooks:**\r\n*   **DocType**: The primary target is a DocType that contains a field linking to the `.md` procedure files. The name is likely `Aesthetic Procedure` or similar.\r\n*   **Hook**: Use the `validate` document event in `hooks.py`. This will automatically trigger the validation logic every time a document of that type is saved, preventing non-compliant entries.\r\n    *   e.g., `doc_events = {\"Aesthetic Procedure\": {\"validate\": \"path.to.validation.method\"}}`\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  In the target DocType's Python controller, define a method (e.g., `validate_procedure_file`).\r\n2.  This method should read the file path from the document's field.\r\n3.  It will then open and parse the content of the Markdown file.\r\n4.  Check for the existence of required sections (Client Preparation, Hygiene, Sterilization, PPE, Assessment Checklist) using regex or a parsing library.\r\n5.  If a section is missing or incomplete, raise `frappe.ValidationError` with a clear message indicating the deficiency.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   The validation logic must handle variations in Markdown formatting (e.g., different heading styles).\r\n*   Implement `try...except` blocks to handle `IOError` for missing files or incorrect paths.\r\n*   For a better user experience on existing documents, consider adding a custom button to the DocType form that triggers the validation manually, rather than only blocking on save.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-012 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis technical brief is for a Claude Code agent tasked with implementing user story US-012 within the `lhdn_payroll_integration` Frappe app.\r\n\r\n**Objective:** Implement a validation system to ensure \"Aesthetic KK\" procedure documents, which are referenced by a Frappe DocType, contain all required sections and details.\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Modify:**\r\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/hooks.py`: To hook the validation logic into a DocType event.\r\n*   `[app]/[doctype]/[doctype].py`: The controller file for the DocType managing the procedures (e.g., `Aesthetic Procedure`). This will house the main validation method.\r\n*   A new utility file (e.g., `lhdn_payroll_integration/utils/validator.py`) could be created to contain the specific Markdown parsing and checking logic, keeping the controller lean.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes & Hooks:**\r\n*   **DocType**: The primary target is a DocType that contains a field linking to the `.md` procedure files. The name is likely `Aesthetic Procedure` or similar.\r\n*   **Hook**: Use the `validate` document event in `hooks.py`. This will automatically trigger the validation logic every time a document of that type is saved, preventing non-compliant entries.\r\n    *   e.g., `doc_events = {\"Aesthetic Procedure\": {\"validate\": \"path.to.validation.method\"}}`\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  In the target DocType's Python controller, define a method (e.g., `validate_procedure_file`).\r\n2.  This method should read the file path from the document's field.\r\n3.  It will then open and parse the content of the Markdown file.\r\n4.  Check for the existence of required sections (Client Preparation, Hygiene, Sterilization, PPE, Assessment Checklist) using regex or a parsing library.\r\n5.  If a section is missing or incomplete, raise `frappe.ValidationError` with a clear message indicating the deficiency.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   The validation logic must handle variations in Markdown formatting (e.g., different heading styles).\r\n*   Implement `try...except` blocks to handle `IOError` for missing files or incorrect paths.\r\n*   For a better user experience on existing documents, consider adding a custom button to the DocType form that triggers the validation manually, rather than only blocking on save.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Story US-012 — Enhance Aesthetic KK practical procedures — treatment techniques and hygiene\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- C01/KK-01: Added Step 1.5 (inspect client gown/slippers for cleanliness/damage); changed surface disinfectant spec to QAC with contact time; added \"ONE DIRECTI","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Jyue-Documents-1-projects-noss-to-wim\\390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9\\tool-results\\b2havuhy3.txt","persistedOutputSize":92488}}
