{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XJtxgXgWkcwZG6wjyF91o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KT(1/3)\n4\t**Muka / Page:** 1\n5\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance\n10\t## Work Activity 1: Carry Out BEV Schedule Maintenance Workplace Preparation\n11\t\n12\t**Reference:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KP(1/3)\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## Soalan / Questions\n17\t\n18\t### Soalan 1 — Multiple Choice (Soalan Aneka Pilihan)\n19\t\n20\tWhich of the following legislation governs occupational safety and health requirements in a BEV maintenance workshop?\n21\t\n22\tA. Road Transport Act 1987 (Act 333)\n23\tB. Environmental Quality Act 1974 (Act 127)\n24\tC. Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994 (Act 514)\n25\tD. Energy Commission Act 2001\n26\t\n27\t### Soalan 2 — Multiple Choice\n28\t\n29\tWhat class rating must insulated gloves have for BEV high voltage work?\n30\t\n31\tA. Class 00 (500V AC)\n32\tB. Class 0 (1000V AC / 1500V DC)\n33\tC. Class 1 (7500V AC)\n34\tD. Class 2 (17000V AC)\n35\t\n36\t### Soalan 3 — True/False (Betul/Salah)\n37\t\n38\tState whether each statement is TRUE or FALSE. Provide justification for FALSE answers.\n39\t\n40\ta) Anti-static flooring is optional in a BEV maintenance workshop.\n41\t\n42\tb) A Class D fire extinguisher is appropriate for lithium battery fires.\n43\t\n44\tc) The hierarchy of controls places PPE as the first line of defence against hazards.\n45\t\n46\td) A Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) must be completed before commencing any BEV maintenance task.\n47\t\n48\t### Soalan 4 — Short Answer (Jawapan Pendek)\n49\t\n50\ta) List FIVE (5) types of hazards found in a BEV workshop environment.\n51\t\n52\tb) Explain the purpose of a toolbox talk (perbincangan peti alat) and list THREE (3) topics that should be covered.\n53\t\n54\tc) Name the FOUR (4) regulatory authorities and their respective legislation that govern BEV maintenance activities in Malaysia.\n55\t\n56\t### Soalan 5 — Matching (Padanan)\n57\t\n58\tMatch each waste type in Column A with the correct storage requirement in Column B.\n59\t\n60\t| Column A (Waste Type) | Column B (Storage Requirement) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9","uuid":"cbbab191-5e1e-4c89-ad6f-5fb75b91d33a","timestamp":"2026-04-17T02:45:37.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C01\\KT-01.md","content":"# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KT(1/3)\n**Muka / Page:** 1\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n\n---\n\n## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance\n## Work Activity 1: Carry Out BEV Schedule Maintenance Workplace Preparation\n\n**Reference:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/KP(1/3)\n\n---\n\n## Soalan / Questions\n\n### Soalan 1 — Multiple Choice (Soalan Aneka Pilihan)\n\nWhich of the following legislation governs occupational safety and health requirements in a BEV maintenance workshop?\n\nA. Road Transport Act 1987 (Act 333)\nB. Environmental Quality Act 1974 (Act 127)\nC. Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994 (Act 514)\nD. Energy Commission Act 2001\n\n### Soalan 2 — Multiple Choice\n\nWhat class rating must insulated gloves have for BEV high voltage work?\n\nA. Class 00 (500V AC)\nB. Class 0 (1000V AC / 1500V DC)\nC. Class 1 (7500V AC)\nD. Class 2 (17000V AC)\n\n### Soalan 3 — True/False (Betul/Salah)\n\nState whether each statement is TRUE or FALSE. Provide justification for FALSE answers.\n\na) Anti-static flooring is optional in a BEV maintenance workshop.\n\nb) A Class D fire extinguisher is appropriate for lithium battery fires.\n\nc) The hierarchy of controls places PPE as the first line of defence against hazards.\n\nd) A Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) must be completed before commencing any BEV maintenance task.\n\n### Soalan 4 — Short Answer (Jawapan Pendek)\n\na) List FIVE (5) types of hazards found in a BEV workshop environment.\n\nb) Explain the purpose of a toolbox talk (perbincangan peti alat) and list THREE (3) topics that should be covered.\n\nc) Name the FOUR (4) regulatory authorities and their respective legislation that govern BEV maintenance activities in Malaysia.\n\n### Soalan 5 — Matching (Padanan)\n\nMatch each waste type in Column A with the correct storage requirement in Column B.\n\n| Column A (Waste Type) | Column B (Storage Requirement) |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":157}}}
