{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ddci9WNotfGKS1AXmdLrdS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Coverage validator for NOSS-to-WIM cross-reference matrix.\n2\t\n3\tUsage:\n4\t    uv run python _tools/coverage_validator.py --subject BEV --output report.txt\n5\t    uv run python _tools/coverage_validator.py --subject all --output report.txt\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n8\t\n9\timport argparse\n10\timport json\n11\timport sys\n12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n13\t\n14\tMATRIX_PATH = Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"_data\" / \"coverage_matrix.json\"\n15\tSUBJECT_KEY_MAP = {\n16\t    \"bev\": \"BEV\",\n17\t    \"aesthetic\": \"Aesthetic\",\n18\t    \"it\": \"IT\",\n19\t}\n20\t\n21\t\n22\tdef check_coverage(subject_key: str, subject_data: dict, project_root: Path) -> dict:\n23\t    \"\"\"Check file existence for one subject and return gap report.\"\"\"\n24\t    folder = project_root / subject_data[\"folder\"]\n25\t    gaps: list[dict] = []\n26\t    covered: list[dict] = []\n27\t\n28\t    for cu_id, cu_data in subject_data[\"CUs\"].items():\n29\t        # Check work activities → KK files\n30\t        for wa in cu_data.get(\"work_activities\", []):\n31\t            kk_path = folder / wa[\"kk_file\"]\n32\t            entry = {\n33\t                \"type\": \"work_activity\",\n34\t                \"noss_code\": wa[\"noss_code\"],\n35\t                \"title\": wa[\"title\"],\n36\t                \"expected_file\": wa[\"kk_file\"],\n37\t                \"cu\": cu_id,\n38\t            }\n39\t            if kk_path.exists():\n40\t                entry[\"status\"] = \"covered\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9","uuid":"99115040-36eb-49cb-a79f-8fcd160dc112","timestamp":"2026-04-17T02:45:59.009Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_tools\\coverage_validator.py","content":"\"\"\"Coverage validator for NOSS-to-WIM cross-reference matrix.\n\nUsage:\n    uv run python _tools/coverage_validator.py --subject BEV --output report.txt\n    uv run python _tools/coverage_validator.py --subject all --output report.txt\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nMATRIX_PATH = Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"_data\" / \"coverage_matrix.json\"\nSUBJECT_KEY_MAP = {\n    \"bev\": \"BEV\",\n    \"aesthetic\": \"Aesthetic\",\n    \"it\": \"IT\",\n}\n\n\ndef check_coverage(subject_key: str, subject_data: dict, project_root: Path) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Check file existence for one subject and return gap report.\"\"\"\n    folder = project_root / subject_data[\"folder\"]\n    gaps: list[dict] = []\n    covered: list[dict] = []\n\n    for cu_id, cu_data in subject_data[\"CUs\"].items():\n        # Check work activities → KK files\n        for wa in cu_data.get(\"work_activities\", []):\n            kk_path = folder / wa[\"kk_file\"]\n            entry = {\n                \"type\": \"work_activity\",\n                \"noss_code\": wa[\"noss_code\"],\n                \"title\": wa[\"title\"],\n                \"expected_file\": wa[\"kk_file\"],\n                \"cu\": cu_id,\n            }\n            if kk_path.exists():\n                entry[\"status\"] = \"covered\"","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":178}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FJQ7Fy9k35rzJd3uT583Zx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now I have the full picture. Let me plan a very compact implementation.\n\n## Current State\n- 85+ KT files across BEV, Aesthetic, IT, and tuinalogy subjects with questions marked by `### Soalan N — Type` or `### Question N — Type` headers\n- Existing tools pattern: Python scripts in `_tools/` with CLI via argparse, tests in `tests/` using subprocess\n- Previous attempt failed: 12453 lines diff (limit 10000). Must keep implementation extremely compact.\n\n## Problem Identified\nNeed a question diversity analyzer that classifies questions by type (MCQ, short answer, scenario, etc.) and reports distribution per subject/CU with recommendations.\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Create `validators/question_diversity_analyzer.py` — compact ~100-line script with `classify_question_type()`, scanning KT files, generating JSON report\n- Create `tests/test_question_diversity_analyzer.py` — compact ~60-line test file\n- Update `prd.json` — mark passes: true\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"validators/question_diversity_analyzer.py\", \"tests/test_question_diversity_analyzer.py\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"prd.json\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"classify_question_type\", \"scan_kt_files\", \"generate_report\", \"main\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 200\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow let me look at a few more KT files to understand question type patterns, then implement."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_read_input_tokens":35696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"390bd59f-ce55-4c9a-9b2a-1ff7d2e0d4e9","uuid":"b30b3a10-d828-420f-bdcc-fe73d1838af6"}
