{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Wdqc5tM5QvTH1vQuo3u7Bu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the question types in the KT files. The headers follow patterns like:\n- `### Soalan N — Type`\n- `### Question N — Type`  \n- `### QN — Type`\n- `### SN — Type`\n- `### Bahagian X: Type` (section-based)\n- Some have no type annotation: `### Soalan N`, `### SN`\n\nTypes found:\n- Multiple Choice / MCQ / Pelbagai Pilihan\n- Short Answer / Jawapan Pendek\n- True/False / Betul/Salah / True or False\n\n\n- Matching / Padanan\n- Scenario / Senario\n- Fill in the Blanks / Isi Tempat Kosong\n- Essay / Esei\n- Diagram Labelling / Rajah / Pelabelan Rajah\n- Calculation / Pengiraan\n- List\n- Practical Writing Task / Tugasan Praktikal\n\nNow I'm planning a compact implementation that keeps the diff minimal—around 120 lines for the analyzer and 80 for tests, avoiding the bloated HTML report that pushed the previous version over 12,000 lines.\n\nI'll output JSON primarily since that satisfies the acceptance criteria, and I can mention that HTML can be generated from it if needed. The real issue is making sure any generated reports go to a temp directory or get gitignored so they don't inflate the diff.\n\nFor the implementation, I need to create the `validators/` directory with the analyzer script and a corresponding test file. I'll keep the analyzer itself lean—around 110 lines—to classify questions by type, calculate distribution percentages, and flag issues like insufficient scenario questions or too many MCQs.\n\nFor the report output, I'll default to JSON and add an optional `--html` flag that generates a minimal HTML wrapper with basic styling around the JSON data, so it satisfies the \"HTML/JSON report\" requirement without bloating the diff.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens"